4|0@9gag^1440856413#cujpgac:DrMonsi$:What exactly are you trying to tell us? As far as I can tell, you are trying to tell us that our "fight" against 9gag is worthless because it happens anyways, so we should just stop uploading stuff to reddit now because it will be on 9gag. So if we don't want 9gag to steal our content, we should just stop uploading stuff to reddit. really? That argument shows such an amount of stupidity that i should not even bother replying to it, but i'm going to do it anyways. There's actually a huge difference between what's shown in the video and what we are "fighting" here on /r/9gag. In the video, the girl posts a picture of herself, and it gets spreaded, and everyone sees her. That sure is bad because the girl probably didn't want this to happen. However, if you upload stuff to reddit, you usually WANT people to see it! you WANT your stuff to go viral, your picture to be seen by people! (there sure are exceptions, but let's leave that aside). So, the point of uploading stuff to reddit is that you WANT people all over the world to see your content, **but**, and here's the thing now, **you want them to be aware that it is YOUR content!**. THIS is what we are fighting here. Most redditors are absolutely fine if you repost their stuff, as long as you mention somewhere where it's coming from. (or at least you tell that you got it from reddit somewhere if you repost stuff on facebook, to name an example). What 9gag does is the complete opposite. they steal your content and tell the world that it is THEIR content. and THIS is what most of us are fighting here. Here's a little story that describes what I mean: imagine you being a small, local fashion designer. you just happen to create a stunning, absolutely faboulous dress. Your dress is so fabulous that people around the city start speaking about it, and it goes "viral". Some days later, you open your favourite fashion magazine with an article about Carl Lagerfeld (or any other famous fashion designer) where he says "hello world, i'm Carl Lagerfeld, here's my latest dress!". But in reality, it is YOUR dress, but Carl Lagerfeld has stolen it and put his initials on it, and is making a whole lot of money out of it. Even your friends are coming to you and tell you "hey, have you seen this absolutely fabulous dress from Carl Lagerfeld? Isn't it amazing?" So, as you see, your video covers a complete different topic. We aren't complaining about 9gag because they are spreading "personal" pictures of ourselves that we don't want others to see, because usually, we want the world to see them. We are fighting 9gag because they tell the world it's THEIR content. They tell the world "hello world, we, 9gag, have created these amazing pictures. have a look. aren't they amazing?". And your neighbours and friends are coming to you and tell you "hey dude, have you seen this picture on 9gag? isn't it amazing? I mean, those 9gag guys, they are amazing!". I guess 99% of all redditors wouldn't mind 9gag reposting their stuff if there was a reddit source link below each stolen picture. So please, think before you post! sincerely, a faggot
